1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:00,960
How’s it going with Moth?

2
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:02,000
Any progress?

3
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:02,960
Are you free tonight?

4
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,200
Can we meet at the same club?

5
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:05,560
I’m setting things up for you.

6
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,760
Find the right moment to talk to Dr. Pun yourself.

7
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,880
So you’re close enough to ask each other out?

8
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:10,840
I’m leaving.

9
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:13,760
You asked me to come.
And now you’re ditching me just like this?

10
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,320
You feel like seeing me now?

11
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,600
Didn’t you say you wanted to hit on me?

12
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:22,920
Isn’t it your birthday today?

13
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,360
Happy birthday.

14
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:17,360
Hey.

15
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:20,720
Moth.

16
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:23,960
Hey there.

17
00:02:28,079 --> 00:02:28,440
We’re here.

18
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,280
When did I fall asleep?

19
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:10,320
I didn’t even realize it.

20
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,920
“Fall asleep” isn’t quite the word.

21
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:15,480
You were plastered.

22
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,280
You still remember?

23
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,400
Or you just completely blacked out?

24
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:55,760
I remember.

25
00:03:58,079 --> 00:03:58,800
I wasn’t that drunk.

26
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,280
Really?

27
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,480
Says the guy who passed out on the cruise.

28
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:06,960
Why did you drink so much?

29
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,920
Well, I had to finish the wine before the ship docked.

30
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,280
Thanks for bringing me home.

31
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,720
Can you make it upstairs on your own?

32
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,040
I can take you up.

33
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,320
I can.

34
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,680
I took a nap. I’m sober now.

35
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:56,280
What?

36
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,600
Just making sure you can get to your room.

37
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:29,720
Can you leave now?

38
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,560
Do you really want me to leave?

39
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,120
First date, and you already
want to get inside my room?

40
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,360
Then…

41
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:51,159
how many dates do we need to go on
before I can get inside?

42
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:00,960
I’m kidding.

43
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,240
This is where I say goodbye.

44
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:04,640
I’m going.

45
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:06,560
Bye-bye.

46
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,240
Happy birthday.

47
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,200
I’m happy…

48
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,320
we got to know each other.

49
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:07,640
Hey.

50
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,200
You like me?

51
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:24,560
Mhm.

52
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,440
I do.

53
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:33,560
So damn much.

54
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:55,000
21 days.

55
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,120
What?

56
00:07:58,159 --> 00:08:01,920
If you truly like me,
go on dates with me for 21 days.

57
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,440
If we make it through all 21 days,

58
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,240
we’ll rethink this.

59
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:15,560
Does that mean after we date for 21 days…

60
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,120
I can get inside your room?

61
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:20,640
Mhm.

62
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,520
Wherever you want to get inside,

63
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:28,960
you can.

64
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:48,240
Are you okay with me…

65
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,440
getting close to Dean?

66
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:53,960
(Mm-hmm.)

67
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:55,480
(Why wouldn’t I be?)

68
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,840
You’re not planning to
get serious with him anyway, right?

69
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,480
(A guy who hits on everyone like Dean)

70
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,760
(and a guy like you who
makes people fall for him at first sight…)

71
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,560
(Of course there’d be sparks.)

72
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:13,840
(But you know this, right?)

73
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:19,000
Relationships are more complicated than that.

74
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:27,120
(Dean isn’t the kind of guy you can stay with for long.)

75
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,640
How long is “long” to you?

76
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,200
For life?

77
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:37,280
I think seven days would be hard enough.

78
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,320
For you and Dean.

79
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:55,760
[I CHANGED MY MIND.]

80
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,080
[LET’S MAKE IT TEN DAYS INSTEAD.]

81
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:04,680
(It may look like love,
but it’s actually just something crazy.)

82
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:08,680
Hey.

83
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,680
I’ve already got Moth to like me.

84
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,920
Now, whether you can make Dr. Pun
your boyfriend or not is up to you.

85
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,480
(Are you sure Moth likes you?)

86
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,320
Well, we kissed.

87
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,240
Is that enough to say he likes me?

88
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:23,200
(Whoa.)

89
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,280
Hey, don’t dump him just yet.

90
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,240
Give me a chance to pursue Dr. Pun first.

91
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,600
Just don’t take too long.

92
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,880
I don’t know how much longer
I can put up with the way he is.

93
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,000
What kind of person is so damn particular?

94
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,560
Yeah. I’m hanging up now.

95
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:46,000
[I CHANGED MY MIND.]
[LET’S MAKE IT TEN DAYS INSTEAD.]

96
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,280
[WHY? YOU THINK YOU CAN’T WAIT?]

97
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:08,880
[WHATEVER YOU SAY :)]

98
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,080
So, where are you?

99
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:36,320
Bailing on me again?

100
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:38,720
I’m here.

101
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:40,920
No need to get fussy.

102
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:45,840
The taxi driver got lost.

103
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:47,720
You planned this date yourself,

104
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:49,880
and you’re the one who’s late.

105
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:51,880
Quit complaining.

106
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:54,960
We agreed we’d take turns
picking what we do on each date.

107
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:56,400
I know.

108
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,560
I remember.

109
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:01,600
I just don’t get why we have to
come to a place like this.

110
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,240
I just want to try it.

111
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:43,280
Hey. I said take a shower.

112
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,120
I know.

113
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:47,440
You do?

114
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,400
Then why are you still wearing your clothes?

115
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:51,800
I’ll take them off later.

116
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,120
Why are you looking at me?

117
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,320
I’m just looking back. You looked at me first.

118
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:58,840
I didn’t.

119
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,480
My eyes were just open.

120
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:06,360
Oh yeah?

121
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,480
Then why are you so shy?

122
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,360
I’m not.

123
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:13,960
You…

124
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:34,680
Happy now?

125
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,400
Hurry up.

126
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,280
Before our time’s up.

127
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:50,800
For beginners, the water temperature
will be 10 to 15 degrees.

128
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,200
I’ll set the timer to five minutes.

129
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,160
If it gets too much, let me know.

130
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,880
If you can’t take it, don’t push yourself.

131
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:12,200
Yeah?

132
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:15,600
Want to compete?

133
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,000
Let’s see who can stay in longer.

134
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:19,240
Bring it.

135
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:20,560
What does the winner get?

136
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,440
Do I get to kiss you again?

137
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,160
Try winning first.

138
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,440
Hey.

139
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,720
If you can’t take it, just give up.

140
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:46,640
No.

141
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,360
Come on.

142
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,840
You don’t want to kiss me that badly?

143
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:51,360
Please.

144
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:54,560
You started it last time.
You bit my lips till they almost split open.

145
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:55,800
I just don’t want to lose.

146
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,120
Yeah?

147
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:58,600
Yeah.

148
00:15:59,040 --> 00:15:59,400
Hey.

149
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,040
I don’t think a kiss is enough.

150
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,480
We’ve already done that, after all.

151
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:08,400
How about we change
the prize to something more than a kiss?

152
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,000
Sounds good?

153
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:11,920
How about a punch?

154
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,240
The winner gets to punch the loser in the face.

155
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,400
Whoa. Punching?

156
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,720
So we’re gonna get it going
and punch each other at the same time?

157
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,440
That’s hot.

158
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,000
The ice feels hotter now.

159
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,360
Ouch.

160
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,080
Hey!

161
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,200
What’s wrong?

162
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,480
Oh. You’re already up?

163
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,560
Does it mean you just lost?

164
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,520
You tricked me?

165
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,600
In sports, that’s called a tactic.

166
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,040
And it’s not against the rules.

167
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:23,240
If you’re mad about losing,
be mad at yourself, not me.

168
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,640
It was a game. It’s normal to get tricky.

169
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:38,760
Normal?

170
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,960
Are you saying it’s normal to play with people’s feelings?

171
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,080
Feelings?

172
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:50,440
What feelings?

173
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,240
I was worried.

174
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,040
Why would you be?

175
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:07,120
Yeah. Screw it.

176
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,240
Actually, you didn’t have to cheat to win.

177
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,160
Not when you’re already so cold-blooded.

178
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:43,920
Late as always.

179
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,000
Only for five minutes.

180
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:49,280
Why’d you reserve such a big table?

181
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:51,800
Hey.

182
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:52,840
Hi.

183
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:54,600
You’re Moth, right?

184
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,840
I’m Ohm. This is Boom.

185
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,400
Mind if we join you?

186
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,080
Hello. Where are you?

187
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,480
Sorry. Traffic was bad.

188
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:03,960
It’s fine.

189
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,000
This is Hun.

190
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,160
And this is Moth.

191
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,520
Ah, so this is him?

192
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,120
I’m hungry.

193
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,440
I’m gonna grab some food.

194
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:14,560
Go ahead.

195
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:18,320
Jo!

196
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:19,320
Over here. Have a seat.

197
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:22,000
How’s it going? Have you been here long?

198
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:22,960
For a while.

199
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:24,840
What is this?

200
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,320
Wasn’t it supposed to be just us?

201
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,400
Don’t be so serious. We’re all friends here.

202
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:52,520
Don’t just eat grapes.

203
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:53,920
They’re good.

204
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:56,240
Have you tried the chicken?

205
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:58,360
I’m going to use the bathroom.

206
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:29,120
The new guy Dean’s seeing is pretty cute.

207
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,240
Too bad he’s a little grumpy.

208
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:36,920
Is it just me, or does he seem a bit arrogant?

209
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,800
Maybe he’s not familiar with us yet.

210
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,680
Or maybe it’s because he’s an artist.

211
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:42,920
Mm.

212
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:48,840
I forgot my phone.

213
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:09,040
[I’M GOING HOME. TIRED!]

214
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:24,720
A date isn’t supposed to be like this.

215
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,360
Keep your chest up.

216
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:29,120
Remember, the waltz is a gentleman’s dance.

217
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,160
Can we dance to the music now?

218
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:38,440
That lunatic can’t stand being alone.

219
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:40,080
He checks his phone every five minutes.

220
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:41,600
And he acts like he knows everyone on earth.

221
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:42,680
You’re exaggerating.

222
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:43,720
Exaggerating, my ass!

223
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:45,240
Just look at all the places he’s taken me.

224
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,000
To paint.

225
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:47,840
To learn dancing.

226
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:48,760
To see art pieces.

227
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:50,080
How is any of that supposed to be a date?

228
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:51,560
Hey, want to eat here?

229
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,960
What’s that? No.

230
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:54,840
It’s delicious. I was so impressed

231
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:56,320
Ew! All I see are bones and chilies.

232
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:57,480
You can eat it yourself.

233
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,680
Maybe he just wanted you to meet his friends.

234
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,240
How about he asks me first if I want to meet them?

235
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,080
Hello. You’re with me on Everydeanlive.

236
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,640
We’re supposed to take things slow.

237
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:09,800
Get to know each other better
before he introduces me to his friends.

238
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,200
How’s he supposed to get to know me…

239
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:14,880
when all he does all day is look at those damn paintings?

240
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,280
He barely says three words to me.

241
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:21,800
And when I take him to meet my friends,
he doesn’t say a word to anyone.

242
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:25,320
If you two really don’t click, why don’t you step back?

243
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:27,120
No! You can’t step back.

244
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,800
I haven’t made any progress with Dr. Pun.

245
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:49,280
I’m hungry.

246
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,560
Want to go eat?

247
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:55,920
If you’re hungry, go ahead.

248
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:02,200
I can wait.

249
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,120
Can we go eat now?

250
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,120
I’ve been waiting for three hours.

251
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:56,680
You can go ahead and eat first.

252
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,240
If you’re going to take this long,

253
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,520
why don’t you take pictures and look at them later?

254
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:09,480
I came all the way here to see the real thing.

255
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:12,200
If I wanted to look at it on my phone,
I could’ve just searched for it online.

256
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,680
Hun booked a table at a shabu place at one p.m.

257
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:18,400
It’s two now.

258
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:20,280
He’s been waiting for an hour.

259
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:28,880
Then go eat with your friends.

260
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:30,960
Why wait for me?

261
00:24:34,120 --> 00:24:34,360
Look.

262
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:36,520
I’m asking you seriously.

263
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:41,360
Why are we even dating
if you’re going to keep ignoring me like this?

264
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:48,560
Who’s ignoring who?

265
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:49,840
You are.

266
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:52,600
Seriously, will there ever be a day

267
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:55,200
when you pay more attention to me
than these fanatical activities?

268
00:24:56,360 --> 00:24:56,600
Hm?

269
00:24:59,160 --> 00:24:59,520
Fanatical?

270
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:01,600
What’s fanatical?

271
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:02,440
Everything.

272
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:03,640
Dance classes.

273
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:05,160
Paintings.

274
00:25:06,920 --> 00:25:08,080
And this ridiculous art.

275
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:12,520
Normal people don’t do this.

276
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:14,360
Only fanatical ones do.

277
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,120
You’re calling me fanatical.

278
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:20,760
What about you?

279
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:23,760
We’re on dates, but all you ever do
is take me to meet your friends.

280
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,800
And all your friends
have hooked up with each other.

281
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,480
Don’t you think it’s dg?

282
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:29,120
What’s dg?

283
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:29,880
Disgusting!

284
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,400
Are you stupid? You seriously didn’t know?

285
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:37,560
Ah!

286
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:42,200
If being smart means pretending to
understand these ridiculous paintings,

287
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,640
then I’m proud to be stupid.

288
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:47,640
Good.

289
00:25:48,520 --> 00:25:51,080
If you know you’re stupid, then stay quiet.

290
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:53,280
Don’t go around calling other people fanatical.

291
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:00,240
Go back to your friends in your little fish tank.

292
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:15,200
Fine. I’m leaving.

293
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:24,040
What are you waiting for?

294
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Cheers!

295
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:52,600
What’s wrong? Why are you so quiet?

296
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:55,400
Nothing.

297
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:56,400
Where’s Moth?

298
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:57,280
Didn’t he come with you?

299
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:58,600
Can you not ask about him?

300
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:00,280
It ruins my mood.

301
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:02,520
Weird.

302
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:06,560
What’s weird?

303
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:09,800
I’ve never seen anyone drive you this crazy before.

304
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:16,440
Are you saying it’s normal to play with people’s feelings?

305
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:17,920
I’m asking seriously.

306
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:21,640
Why are we even dating if
you’re going to keep ignoring me like this?

307
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:45,000
Yeah?

308
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:46,760
(Where are you?)

309
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:48,680
I just got home.

310
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:51,760
I saw you unfollowed Dean on Instagram.

311
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:56,040
(Are you okay?)

312
00:27:57,720 --> 00:27:58,280
Of course I am.

313
00:27:59,560 --> 00:28:01,320
Do you really think
I’d be upset over something like this?

314
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:07,960
I know you care about me, Pun.

315
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:11,280
But you should know that I’m okay.

316
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:16,120
Can I be honest with you?

317
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:20,080
I don’t think you’re okay at all, Moth.

318
00:28:27,280 --> 00:28:30,120
Listen. I’m not rooting for Dean or anything.

319
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:37,280
But if you really want to open yourself up
and let someone into your life,

320
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:42,560
(you can’t keep doing things the way you always have.)

321
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:44,800
What do you mean?

322
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:47,440
You mean I should stop being myself?

323
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:49,480
Stop doing what I want

324
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:52,520
and force myself to do silly things just to please someone else?

325
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,520
That’s so damn crazy.

326
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:59,760
(Making adjustments isn’t crazy.)

327
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:04,160
(You know what’s crazy?)

328
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,440
(You.)

329
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:12,800
(When you’re with someone,
you never tone yourself down for anyone.)

330
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:15,880
Think about it.

331
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:23,880
(In all your past relationships,
you always set rules and conditions.)

332
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:30,880
(It’s like they had to complete a bunch of quests
just to earn a place in your life.)

333
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:35,200
And you know what?

334
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:41,640
In every game you forced them to play,
you never allowed yourself to lose.

335
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,520
You always had to win every game, every time.

336
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:50,560
Does it mean you just lost?

337
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:53,440
If you’re hungry, go ahead.

338
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,120
I can wait.

339
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:02,760
If you know you’re stupid, then stay quiet.

340
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:13,960
Fine. I’m leaving.

341
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:17,280
What are you waiting for?

342
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:24,040
(That’s what I think is so unhinged.)

343
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:38,040
Please.

344
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:43,240
In the future, if you're going to give a chance to…

345
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,960
someone and let them into your life,

346
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,080
(can you stop setting conditions)

347
00:30:57,320 --> 00:31:02,480
(and just let things happen based on how you feel?)

348
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:27,720
Hey.

349
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:28,480
I’m gonna leave now.

350
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:29,720
I’m tired.

351
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:33,440
Dean.

352
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:35,640
Going to the bathroom?

353
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:37,080
No, bro.

354
00:31:37,280 --> 00:31:37,600
I’m leaving.

355
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,360
What’s wrong with him?

356
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:47,560
Heartbroken.

357
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:49,040
Dean? Heartbroken?

358
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:57,680
What crazy shit are you talking about?

359
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:58,960
What’s crazy?

360
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:03,080
What I said, or your feelings going crazy?

361
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:11,160
Fighting your feelings too much can drive you nuts.

362
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:16,200
Just accept your feelings
and figure out how to deal with them.

363
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:18,040
That’s the best thing you can do.

364
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:29,280
Okay.

365
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,280
I’ll accept that…

366
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,080
I really like Moth.

367
00:32:39,120 --> 00:32:40,440
Just like you liked everyone else before him?

368
00:32:48,600 --> 00:32:49,840
I stand by what I said.

369
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:54,240
It looks to me more like you’re falling in love.

370
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,160
Why are you here?

371
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:25,400
I saw Hun’s Story and figured you’d be here.

372
00:33:49,800 --> 00:33:50,880
Why didn’t you call if you wanted to talk?

373
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:55,800
Well, I wanted to talk in person more.

374
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:02,440
How come you know Hun’s IG?

375
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:07,240
He followed me since that day at the buffet place.

376
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:11,000
Good that you accepted his follow request.

377
00:34:12,120 --> 00:34:14,120
I thought you wouldn’t become friends
with anyone else in the world.

378
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:22,760
Look.

379
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,639
I don’t have any problem with your friends.

380
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:30,440
Actually, every one of them is nice.

381
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:32,760
But…

382
00:34:36,159 --> 00:34:36,840
Never mind.

383
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:45,440
Let’s just say that if I meet your friends again,

384
00:34:49,719 --> 00:34:53,719
I will try not to put up my walls around them.

385
00:35:01,040 --> 00:35:01,360
Why?

386
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:03,920
Do you still want to meet them?

387
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:06,720
I didn’t say I wanted to meet them.

388
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:09,280
I said if I met them again.

389
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,040
So that means…

390
00:35:18,760 --> 00:35:19,720
our date continues?

391
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:25,200
Well…

392
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:28,840
What do you say?

393
00:35:38,240 --> 00:35:40,480
Honestly, I didn’t know what was on your mind.

394
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:46,040
I just thought it wouldn’t hurt to

395
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:52,560
introduce you to my friends and bring you into my world.

396
00:35:57,760 --> 00:36:01,360
But if you’d just told me directly what you didn’t like

397
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:06,240
or who you didn’t want to see,

398
00:36:09,320 --> 00:36:11,960
it would’ve been easier than trying to guess, right?

399
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:23,040
Not to mention, you acted likeyou didn’t care about me.

400
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:26,600
I’m sorry.

401
00:36:29,160 --> 00:36:31,600
I was at fault too for not being considerate enough.

402
00:36:34,280 --> 00:36:37,640
I forgot that you’re a different type of human than I am.

403
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:46,880
It’s not just that.

404
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:53,720
I’m sorry for always saying harsh things to you.

405
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:07,160
I didn’t know what you thought about
the way I expressed myself,

406
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,480
but going on dates with you…

407
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:15,120
was good.

408
00:37:24,560 --> 00:37:26,280
I’ve always wanted to learn ballroom dancing.

409
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:30,200
But I never had the guts to try because

410
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:33,360
I was afraid I’d have to dance with someone I didn’t know.

411
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:38,680
And I’d never been able to go to workshops

412
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:42,320
or look at art in peace

413
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:45,960
because people always approached me.

414
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:53,600
But when I was with you,
no one dared come over and flirt with me.

415
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:03,840
Okay, sometimes we didn’t click

416
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:06,280
or got on each other’s nerves,

417
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:12,960
but overall, I had a good time.

418
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:17,560
It was more than okay to go on dates with you.

419
00:38:25,480 --> 00:38:29,800
So, I never felt like you weren’t important.

420
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:36,040
I’m really sorry
I gave you the wrong impression.

421
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:46,160
Next time, you can just let me know.

422
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:39,480
Hey.

423
00:39:40,120 --> 00:39:40,840
I thought you left.

424
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:43,560
Moth wanted to come.

425
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:45,720
I changed my mind. Sorry.

426
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:49,800
Mind if I join you guys?

427
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:54,800
Of course. Come on.

428
00:39:55,120 --> 00:39:57,560
Let’s start with a welcome drink.

429
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:00,280
That’s not enough.

430
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:03,080
No.

431
00:40:03,720 --> 00:40:05,360
Just a little, so you can catch up with us.

432
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:13,800
There!

433
00:40:14,320 --> 00:40:15,200
Hey, wait.

434
00:40:16,240 --> 00:40:16,840
Dean.

435
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:18,480
Your glass is still right here.

436
00:40:20,120 --> 00:40:20,560
Glad you didn’t forget about it.

437
00:40:21,680 --> 00:40:23,000
Cheers!

438
00:40:48,520 --> 00:40:49,080
(That’s right.)

439
00:40:50,680 --> 00:40:52,280
(It all started with something crazy.)

440
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:59,280
(And I honestly don’t know
where this craziness will take me,)

441
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:04,680
(or how it will end.)

442
00:41:09,440 --> 00:41:10,920
(Should I call it love?)

443
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:18,640
(Or maybe…)

444
00:41:20,160 --> 00:41:21,440
(they’ve always been one and the same.)

445
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:52,360
Are you going to black out again this time?

446
00:41:54,640 --> 00:41:55,080
No.

447
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:57,240
I didn’t drink that much.

448
00:42:00,040 --> 00:42:01,200
Who are you, really?

449
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:04,680
What do you mean?

450
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:07,920
You’re antisocial. Like, an introvert.

451
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:12,480
But most introverts I know don’t drink like you do.

452
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:13,960
Ten, for example.

453
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:17,040
All he does all day is hang out with his dog.

454
00:42:18,480 --> 00:42:18,880
So what?

455
00:42:20,520 --> 00:42:25,640
Are introverts supposed to just make matcha
and read at home?

456
00:42:26,720 --> 00:42:28,520
Can’t they go out to enjoy the nightlife
and have a few drinks?

457
00:42:31,560 --> 00:42:35,080
Besides, I’ve never considered myself an introvert.

458
00:42:36,080 --> 00:42:36,800
Then what are you?

459
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:40,720
Um…

460
00:42:42,200 --> 00:42:46,640
A maniac, I guess.

461
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:59,520
Actually, I like being in crowded places.

462
00:43:01,480 --> 00:43:05,000
As long as no one comes and bothers me.

463
00:43:06,360 --> 00:43:07,120
Super ironic.

464
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:09,760
What?

465
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:11,640
It’s true.

466
00:43:13,640 --> 00:43:14,200
That’s not that.

467
00:43:15,840 --> 00:43:20,680
I just didn’t expect someone like you
to say things like that.

468
00:43:23,240 --> 00:43:24,280
Well, I read a lot.

469
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:33,760
So, how many days of dating do we have left?

470
00:43:34,280 --> 00:43:34,920
Two?

471
00:43:35,800 --> 00:43:36,280
Three.

472
00:43:43,440 --> 00:43:45,160
(Can you stop setting conditions)

473
00:43:46,480 --> 00:43:52,520
(and just let things happen based on how you feel?)

474
00:43:57,680 --> 00:43:58,200
What?

475
00:44:29,080 --> 00:44:29,640
Wait.

476
00:44:45,080 --> 00:44:46,320
You can stop hitting on Moth.

477
00:44:46,720 --> 00:44:48,200
I have to accept that…

478
00:44:48,520 --> 00:44:51,120
things between him and me can only go so far.

479
00:44:51,280 --> 00:44:51,880
Shit.

480
00:44:52,080 --> 00:44:53,320
You don’t have to be so harsh.

481
00:44:53,680 --> 00:44:54,320
Why are you following me?

482
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:55,080
Aren’t you going home?

483
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:56,360
I am going home.

484
00:44:56,800 --> 00:44:59,200
Your head line and your heart line meet.

485
00:44:59,200 --> 00:45:00,440
It means you’re stubborn.

486
00:45:01,200 --> 00:45:01,760
But cute.

487
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:04,880
Who would get serious with Dean unless they’re an idiot?

488
00:45:05,400 --> 00:45:06,640
I’m not getting serious with Dean anyway.

489
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:10,760
Do you like it soft or rough?
